     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "'Story:\\nIn a remote part of the Amazon rainforest, a wildlife conservationist named Clara has established a small tamarin sanctuary where injured and orphaned tamarins are rehabilitated and eventually released back into their natural habitat. Using only the clues below, match each tamarin at the sanctuary with its age and caretaker, and determine where each animal was originally found. Remember, as with all grid-based logic puzzles, no option in any category will ever be used more than once. If you get stuck or run into problems, try the \"Clear Errors\" button to remove any mistakes that might be present on the grid, or the \"Hint\" button to see the next logical step in the puzzle.\\n\\nClues:\\n1.The 5-year-old is either the animal Lila works with or the tamarin Mika works with.\\n2.Pipoca is 9 years old.\\n3.Tamara is 4 years older than the animal Mika works with.\\n4.The tamarin Nia works with is younger than Zephyr.\\n5.Of the tamarin Bella works with and the 14-year-old, one is Pipoca and the other is Tamara.\\n6.The 14-year-old is cared for by Clara.\\n\\nSolve the grid puzzle by filling the table:\\n+--------+--------------+------------+\\n|   Ages | Tamarins     | Caretakers |\\n+========+==============+============+\\n|      5 |              |            |\\n+--------+--------------+------------+\\n|      7 |              |            |\\n+--------+++-------------+------------+\\n|      9 |              |            |\\n+--------+--------------+------------+\\n|     12 |              |            |\\n+--------+--------------+------------+\\n|     14 |              |            |\\n+--------+--------------+------------+\\n\\nUse the clues to fill the table with the following categories:\\nTamarins: Bella, Nia, Mika, Pipoca, Tamara\\nCaretakers: Lila, Zephyr, Dora, Eva, Clara'"
      ]
